# Every change needs maintainer review, but the paths below are the ones where a
# mistake is a vulnerability rather than a bug. Listing them separately makes that
# visible in the pull request UI and prevents a drive-by merge.

*                           @mdferdousalam

# The cryptographic core and the on-disk format: a mistake here is
# unrecoverable for anyone who already saved a vault.
/crates/keel-crypto/        @mdferdousalam
/crates/keel-format/        @mdferdousalam

# The only crate permitted `unsafe`.
/crates/keel-hardening/     @mdferdousalam

# The only process that holds unlocked keys, plus the policy chokepoint.
/crates/keel-agent/         @mdferdousalam
/crates/keel-core/          @mdferdousalam

# Editing these edits a security boundary that CI enforces.
/xtask/src/rules.rs         @mdferdousalam
/deny.toml                  @mdferdousalam

# Release integrity: the signing and provenance flow.
/.github/workflows/         @mdferdousalam
